<https://bioregistry.io/registry/ohdab> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Based on the classification of occupations (KldB) by the Federal Employment Agency and the Federal Statistical Office from 2010. This in turn is based on the International Standard Classification of Occupations (ISCO) by the International Labor Office (ILO 2008). The KldB was revised and expanded in parts at the Historical Data Center in Halle, making it usable for the classification of historical occupations. More than 44,000 historical occupations are taxonomically classified in the OhdAB and can be sorted into occupational areas, main occupational groups, or variously differentiated occupational groups."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
