<https://bioregistry.io/registry/homd.seq> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The Human Oral Microbiome Database (HOMD) provides a site-specific comprehensive database for the more than 600 prokaryote species that are present in the human oral cavity. It contains genomic information based on a curated 16S rRNA gene-based provisional naming scheme, and taxonomic information. This datatype contains genomic sequence information."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
