<https://bioregistry.io/registry/nif.grossanatomy> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The \"Neuroscience Information Framework Gross Anatomy\" was developed as part of the NIF Standard Ontologies. It extended NeuroNames by including terms from BIRNLex, SumsDB, BrainMap.org, etc.; for multi-scale\nrepresentation of the nervous system and macroscopic anatomy. For more information, see the article  \"Development and use of Ontologies Inside the Neuroscience Information Framework: A Practical Approach\" \nFT Imam et al, Front Genet 2012 Jun 22; 3:111. doi: 10.3389/fgene.2012.00111. eCollection 2012 https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22737162/"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
