<https://bioregistry.io/registry/obcs> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "OBCS stands for the Ontology of Biological and Clinical Statistics. OBCS is an ontology in the domain of biological and clinical statistics. It is aligned with the Basic Formal Ontology (BFO) and the Ontology for Biomedical Investigations (OBI)"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://bioregistry.io/registry/gwascentral.marker> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "GWAS Central (previously the Human Genome Variation database of Genotype-to-Phenotype information) is a database of summary level findings from genetic association studies, both large and small. It gathers datasets from public domain projects, and accepts direct data submission. It is based upon Marker information encompassing SNP and variant information from public databases, to which allele and genotype frequency data, and genetic association findings are additionally added. A Study (most generic level) contains one or more Experiments, one or more Sample Panels of test subjects, and one or more Phenotypes. This collection references a GWAS Central Marker."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
