<https://bioregistry.io/registry/crisprdb> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Repeated CRISPR (\"clustered regularly interspaced short palindromic repeats\") elements found in archaebacteria and eubacteria are believed to defend against viral infection, potentially targeting invading DNA for degradation. CRISPRdb is a database that stores information on CRISPRs that are automatically extracted from newly released genome sequence data."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
