<https://bioregistry.io/registry/emaps> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "EMAPA identifiers refer to developmental stage-independent mouse anatomical features, for instance, EMAPA:35178 resolves to the MGI's Mouse Developmental Anatomy Browser. EMAPS is an extension to EMAPA which introduces terms for different developmental stages of this generic EMAPA entry. EMAPS identifiers are constructed such that they are a concatenation of the EMAPA ID and a Theiler Stage (TS) number. For instance, EMAPA:35178 in TS 23 becomes EMAPS:3517823"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
