<https://bioregistry.io/registry/gmho> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The GALENOS Mental Health Ontology (GMHO) is being developed to represent the full range of concepts relevant to mental health. It forms a core component of the Global Alliance for Living Evidence on aNxiety, depressiOn and pSychosis (GALENOS) project, which aims to build a living evidence base for anxiety, depression, and psychosis.\nThe GMHO is designed to structure and organise evidence drawn from multiple living systematic reviews, supporting the creation of a structured data repository that enables clearer synthesis, integration, and retrieval of research findings. Its upper-level framework is intentionally designed for reuse, providing a general foundation for organising evidence across the broader mental health domain."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
